Description: Estimates the total burden of recurrent events within a population
    using the Mean Cumulative Count (MCC) method described by Dong et al. (2015)
    <doi:10.1093/aje/kwu289>. The package handles left-truncated data in the
    presence of competing risks by applying time-dependent censoring and
    truncation weights following Geskus (2011)
    <doi:10.1111/j.1541-0420.2010.01420.x>, with bootstrap confidence intervals,
    visualization with number-at-risk tables, and simulation utilities for
    complex cohort studies.
